    "It is built on a heavy-duty thick-plate flooded design with a lead-antimony (Pb-Sb) grid. This is a deliberate engineering choice over the thinner calcium-alloy plates used in passenger cars — antimony tolerates the deep cycling, high current draw and constant vibration of large diesel engines, at the cost of requiring occasional water top-up (a serviceable design, not a defect).",
